<h1>Kara Tools</h1>
<p><a href="https://ci.example.com/kara"><img src="https://ci.example.com/badge.svg" alt="build" /></a>
A set of <em>small</em>, <strong>fast</strong> command-line tools for working with logs,
config files and archives. See the <a href="guide.md">guide</a> and the
<a href="CHANGELOG.md#unreleased">changelog</a> for details.</p>
<h2>Install</h2>
<p>Download a release, or build from source:</p>
<pre><code class="language-sh">git clone https://example.com/kara-tools.git
cd kara-tools &amp;&amp; make install PREFIX=~/.local
</code></pre>
<p>You need:</p>
<ul>
<li>a C compiler (<code>cc</code> or <code>clang</code>)</li>
<li>GNU make 4.0 or newer</li>
<li>about 50 MB of disk</li>
</ul>
<h2>Usage</h2>
<pre><code>kt grep -i error app.log
kt toml check Cargo.toml
</code></pre>
<p>Every tool reads <code>stdin</code> when no file is given, and exits with status
<code>1</code> when it finds nothing. Flags follow the usual rules:</p>
<ol>
<li>Short flags combine: <code>-iv</code> is <code>-i -v</code>.</li>
<li>A <code>--</code> ends the flags.</li>
<li>Long flags take <code>=</code>: <code>--color=never</code>.</li>
</ol>
<h2>Contributing</h2>
<p>Bug reports are welcome at <a href="https://example.com/kara-tools/issues">https://example.com/kara-tools/issues</a>.
Please read <a href="https://example.com/kara-tools/CONTRIBUTING" title="How to contribute">the contributing notes</a> first, and run the tests
with <code>make check</code>.</p>
<p>Licensed under the MIT license. Copyright (c) 2026 the Kara authors.</p>
