<h1>User guide</h1>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Note:</strong> this guide covers version 1.4. Commands marked <em>(new)</em> need
the unreleased build.</p>
</blockquote>
<h2>Searching logs</h2>
<p>The <code>kt grep</code> command takes a pattern and a list of files:</p>
<pre><code class="language-console">$ kt grep -c &quot;timeout&quot; /var/log/app/*.log
app-1.log:3
app-2.log:0
</code></pre>
<p>A pattern is matched against each line. These rules apply:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Matching is case-sensitive unless you pass <code>-i</code>.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>A pattern that starts with <code>-</code> must follow <code>--</code>.</p>
<p>For example, <code>kt grep -- -v notes.txt</code> searches for <code>-v</code>.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Use <code>-e `pat` </code> to pass a pattern holding backticks.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3>Exit codes</h3>
<ol start="3">
<li>Found at least one match: the status is <code>0</code>.</li>
<li>Found nothing: the status is <code>1</code>.</li>
<li>An error: the status is <code>2</code>.</li>
</ol>
<h2>Rotating files</h2>
<p>To rotate <code>app.log</code> when it reaches 10 MB, keeping five old copies:</p>
<pre><code>kt rotate --size 10M --keep 5 app.log
</code></pre>
<p>Rotation renames <code>app.log</code> to <code>app.log.1</code>, shifts the older copies up
by one, and deletes the copy past the limit.<br />
The rename is atomic, so a reader never sees a missing file.</p>
<h2>Emphasis, briefly</h2>
<p>Text can be <em>emphasised</em>, <em>also like this</em>, or <strong>strong</strong>. Mixed forms
nest: <em><strong>both at once</strong></em>, <em>emphasis with <strong>strong</strong> inside</em>, and
<strong>strong with <em>emphasis</em> inside</strong>. Underscores inside words do not
count, so <code>snake_case_name</code> and snake_case_name stay as they are, and
2 * 3 * 4 is arithmetic. A literal *star* needs a backslash.</p>
<p>Two spaces at the end of a line<br />
make a hard break.</p>
<h2>Images and links</h2>
<p><img src="img/arch.png" alt="Architecture diagram" title="How the tools fit together" /></p>
<p>Links can be <a href="https://example.com/docs" title="Docs home">inline</a>,
<a href="https://example.com/ref">by reference</a>, <a href="https://example.com/collapsed">collapsed</a> or just <a href="https://example.com/shortcut" title="Shortcut title">shortcut</a>. A path with
spaces needs angle brackets: <a href="docs/release%20notes.md">notes</a>.</p>
<hr />
<p>Questions? Open an issue.</p>
